+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_01NL3JmSt1SroKptWKh7iyrY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RXgMAktDxwSkHcEYhuEdCm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# Contract: Versioned Document Store with Structural Merge\n\nVerification: `npm test` (vitest) unless noted. Each criterion below maps to one or more\ntests in `src/*.test.ts`.\n\n## Design decisions (spec is silent / ambiguous on these)\n- Re-creating a document after it was `delete`d is allowed (its version lineage continues\n  from the pre-delete version) — matches common \"un-delete via create\" CRUD expectations.\n- `getHistory` on a deleted document still returns its pre-delete history; it only throws\n  if the id never existed on the current branch.\n- `create`/`update` validate that `content` is a non-null, non-array object (per the\n  \"documents are plain JSON objects\" constraint) and throw `TypeError` otherwise.\n- Merge is atomic across documents in a single `merge()` call: if ANY document produces a\n  conflict, `applied` is `false` and NO document on the target branch is changed, even ones\n  that merged cleanly.\n- `merged` includes every document that is live (not deleted/absent) in the merge result,\n  for every document id known to either branch — this represents \"what the resulting branch\n  would look like,\" not just the ones that had field-level changes.\n- Delete-vs-modify (one branch deletes a document the other branch edited) is reported as a\n  single whole-document conflict with `path: \"\"`, `ours`/`theirs` being `null` for the\n  deleted side.\n- Three-way merge recurses into nested plain objects at any depth, producing dot-separated\n  paths (e.g. `a.b.c`) for conflicts found at nested levels. Arrays and primitives are\n  compared atomically (whole-value), not diffed internally.\n\n## Documents (CRUD)\n- [ ] `create(id, content)` stores a doc retrievable via `get(id)` 