+# Contract: Versioned Document Store with Structural Merge
+
+Verification: `npm test` (vitest) unless noted. Each criterion below maps to one or more
+tests in `src/*.test.ts`.
+
+## Design decisions (spec is silent / ambiguous on these)
+- Re-creating a document after it was `delete`d is allowed (its version lineage continues
+  from the pre-delete version) — matches common "un-delete via create" CRUD expectations.
+- `getHistory` on a deleted document still returns its pre-delete history; it only throws
+  if the id never existed on the current branch.
+- `create`/`update` validate that `content` is a non-null, non-array object (per the
+  "documents are plain JSON objects" constraint) and throw `TypeError` otherwise.
+- Merge is atomic across documents in a single `merge()` call: if ANY document produces a
+  conflict, `applied` is `false` and NO document on the target branch is changed, even ones
+  that merged cleanly.
+- `merged` includes every document that is live (not deleted/absent) in the merge result,
+  for every document id known to either branch — this represents "what the resulting branch
+  would look like," not just the ones that had field-level changes.
+- Delete-vs-modify (one branch deletes a document the other branch edited) is reported as a
+  single whole-document conflict with `path: ""`, `ours`/`theirs` being `null` for the
+  deleted side.
+- Three-way merge recurses into nested plain objects at any depth, producing dot-separated
+  paths (e.g. `a.b.c`) for conflicts found at nested levels. Arrays and primitives are
+  compared atomically (whole-value), not diffed internally.
+
+## Documents (CRUD)
+- [ ] `create(id, content)` stores a doc retrievable via `get(id)` → test: create + get roundtrip
+- [ ] `create` throws when id already exists (not deleted) on current branch → test: double create throws
+- [ ] `create` throws (TypeError) when content is not a plain object (array/null/primitive) → test: invalid content rejected
+- [ ] `get` throws when id was never created → test: get unknown id throws
+- [ ] `get` throws when id was deleted → test: get after delete throws
+- [ ] `get` returns a deep clone (mutating the returned object does not affect the store) → test: mutate returned object, get again, unaffected
+- [ ] `update(id, content)` replaces content, visible via `get` → test: update then get reflects new content
+- [ ] `update` throws when id doesn't exist / was deleted → test: update unknown / deleted id throws
+- [ ] `delete(id)` removes the doc; subsequent `get` throws → test: delete then get throws
+- [ ] `delete` throws when id doesn't exist / already deleted → test: double delete throws
+- [ ] Re-`create` after `delete` succeeds and is retrievable → test: delete then create then get
+
+## Version history
+- [ ] `create` and `update` each add one version with unique `id`, numeric `timestamp`, full `content` → test: history length grows by 1 per op, ids unique
+- [ ] `getHistory(id)` returns versions oldest-first → test: create + 2 updates, history[0] is original, history[2] is latest
+- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns that version's content → test: fetch each historical version, content matches what was stored at that point
+- [ ] `getVersion` throws for unknown versionId or versionId belonging to a different doc → test: cross-doc / bogus version id throws
+- [ ] History content is deep-cloned (independent of live doc mutations) → test: update doc after fetching history entry, history entry unchanged
+
+## Branching
+- [ ] Default branch is `"main"` → test: `getBranch()` on fresh store returns `"main"`
+- [ ] `createBranch(name)` branches from current branch's current state → test: branch inherits existing docs
+- [ ] `createBranch(name, fromBranch)` branches from the named branch instead → test: branch from non-current branch
+- [ ] `createBranch` throws if branch name already exists → test: duplicate branch name throws
+- [ ] `createBranch` throws if `fromBranch` doesn't exist → test: unknown fromBranch throws
+- [ ] `switchBranch(name)` changes the active branch; throws if unknown → test: switch + getBranch reflects it; unknown branch throws
+- [ ] `listBranches()` includes all created branches → test: create a few, check membership
+- [ ] Changes on one branch are invisible on another → test: create/update/delete doc on branch A, absent/unaffected on branch B
+- [ ] Branch history is independently versioned after divergence → test: same doc edited differently on two branches, histories diverge
+
+## Merge — no-conflict paths
+- [ ] Merging a branch with no changes since fork is a no-op, `applied: true`, no new versions created on target → test: immediate merge after branch creation
+- [ ] Field changed only on source branch is taken → test: theirs-only field change auto-applied
+- [ ] Field changed only on target branch is kept → test: ours-only field change auto-applied
+- [ ] Same field changed to the same value on both branches → no conflict → test: identical concurrent edits merge cleanly
+- [ ] Independent documents changed on each branch merge cleanly with no conflicts → test: doc A changed on ours, doc B changed on theirs, both present after merge
+- [ ] Nested object field changes merge at the leaf level (non-conflicting siblings preserved) → test: ours edits a.x, theirs edits a.y, both present after merge
+- [ ] New document created only on source branch is added to target after merge → test: create-only-on-theirs document appears after merge
+- [ ] Document deleted on source (unchanged on target) is deleted on target after successful merge → test: delete-on-theirs applied
+- [ ] Successful merge creates a new version in target branch history for every changed doc → test: getHistory grows after merge for affected doc
+- [ ] `merge` throws if sourceBranch doesn't exist → test: unknown source branch throws
+
+## Merge — conflict paths
+- [ ] Same field changed to different values on both branches → conflict with correct path/base/ours/theirs → test: scalar field conflict
+- [ ] Conflict path is dot-separated for nested fields → test: nested field conflict reports "a.b.c"-style path
+- [ ] When any conflict exists, `applied` is `false` and target branch is completely unchanged (including non-conflicting docs from the same merge call) → test: mixed clean-doc + conflicting-doc merge leaves both untouched
+- [ ] `merged` result reflects "ours" resolution for conflicting fields, "theirs"/"ours" resolution for non-conflicting ones, even when `applied: false` → test: inspect merged content on a conflicting merge
+- [ ] Delete-vs-modify conflict reported at document level (`path: ""`) → test: one branch deletes, other edits same doc
+
+## Integration
+- [ ] Full scenario: branch, diverge, merge clean, merge conflicting, resolve manually via update → test: end-to-end story
